BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (the green LED lights [JCDyzlYC0h0 @ 00:01:08]. Jim Mack stays fully manual, laying a straight edge across two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (shoes and reading a CAT 5P3277 ruler for 1.68 inches of grouser and 3.54 inches of link height, then averaging several) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (locations instead of trusting a single spot [YyZcRwETdeA @ 00:00:34].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Pitch and sprocket calls are where the specs diverge hardest. C&C Equipment measures center of pin to center of pin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (over four links against a 761 millimeter new figure, logs 762 as 15 percent worn, and deliberately repeats the reading in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (a second spot because the chain may be taking up or sucked together at one end [Hif9qgd9EEI @ 00:04:49]. Volvo's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (inspector says the span depends on who built the undercarriage, anywhere from five, four or three pins, and the number) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (only means something once it runs through that maker's conversion chart for life used or remaining [L3kAdkTSgI4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (00:03:05]. Komatsu Australia demands a tight track before the tape goes on and measures across five pins or four links,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (checking several points around the chain [JCDyzlYC0h0 @ 00:02:14]. Sprockets split the room again. C&C has no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (number at all and reads them by eye: a flat middle with roughly a half inch of room is healthy, and a sharp point means) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (they are done. Hunter Valley Tracks, by contrast, runs a tape across three teeth of one segment, plugs that into its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (undercarriage program alongside link height, bush thickness, rollers, idlers and shoe lug height, and converts the lot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (into wear rates [1B6uxG5WNzQ @ 00:00:36].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (Oil sampling has its own competing playbooks. Shelly Eckert of Chevron calls a sampling valve on the engine block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (the industry standard because the sample comes from the exact same place every time, with the vampire pump threaded) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (down the dipstick to the sump as the fallback [QYimn88ydQI @ 00:09:35]. WearCheck agrees the sample port is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (preferred and that the machine must be running for oil pressure, but also teaches a dipstick-pump method, with tubing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (measured to the dipstick plus about a foot and cut at 45 degrees, and a mid-drain grab after several gallons have run out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm ([ypiqyyCR9MI @ 00:02:43]. Timing and fill rules differ too. Mike Dudley at Carter Machinery wants about 20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (minutes of operation so the fluid is fully homogenized, and sampling every 250 hours unless the maintenance guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (calls for something else [R9dHZ4P7yp0 @ 00:01:08], while WearCheck pulls within a few minutes of shutdown and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (stops at two-thirds to three-quarters full. Jeff Payne at Caterpillar fills to the printed line, but only after pulling a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (throwaway clean-out sample first, because dust sitting in the little hole at the end of the valve contaminates the first) Tj ET
