BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Henderson Heavy Haul out of Grand Junction, Colorado [qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:04:13]. Loaded, the rig ran 125 feet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (long and 250,000 pounds, which made it a superload. Arizona required permits, pilot cars, and four state police on a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (night move that started at 10 p.m. Trinity Logistics confirms that extra-wide loads can trigger law enforcement escorts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (in some states, with their time usually paid by the hauling company [oQI9qiLLIwA @ 00:01:46]. Woods itemizes pilot) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (pricing. The chase car bills $1.65 a mile, $85 per overnight, $250 a day plus hotel on a no-go, and a day rate near $600) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (when it moves under 300 miles. The pole car runs $1.85 to $2 a mile with a higher day rate because pole cars are harder) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (to find [qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:09:06]. Nevada bans weekend travel, so arriving Friday meant three no-go days at $250) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (each, about $1,000 with hotels, while the pilots played keno. The Kenworth W990 pulling the load gets only about 1.8) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (miles per gallon on the crawls [qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:10:19].) Tj ET
