BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.00 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 493.77 Tm (The costliest heavy-haul mistakes in Scott Woods's files are bidding errors. One broker bid a load without knowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 478.55 Tm (pilot cars were required, lost about five grand on the move, and watched the truck hold the load hostage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 463.32 Tm ([qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:03:03]. Former students who folded crane rigging into the job without understanding it lost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.10 Tm ($25,000 to $30,000 on a single load. Timing breaks naive bids too: the Washington permit on the Cat 777 move took) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 432.87 Tm (three weeks, superloads can wait three weeks to a month, and 500,000-pound moves on 30-axle trailers can sit four) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 417.65 Tm (months while states run route surveys [qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:15:56]. Mileage lies on the bid sheet, because PC Miler) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 402.42 Tm (may show 863 miles while the state-issued route runs 1,700 [qHs0sXdzamw @ 00:18:13]. Weekend curfews add dead) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.20 Tm (cost on multi-state runs: Nevada bars weekend travel, so pilot cars sat Friday through Sunday at $250 a day plus hotels,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.97 Tm (roughly another $1,000 for doing nothing. The truck's 1,200-mile deadhead to Gillette, Wyoming, also lands in the rate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 356.75 Tm (whether the broker sees it or not. Trinity Logistics adds the enforcement edge: exact routes must be specified on each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 341.52 Tm (state permit, and missing a permit or breaking its conditions can bring significant fines [oQI9qiLLIwA @ 00:03:10].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 326.30 Tm (On the fleet side, Yvette Aubin names the missing preventive and predictive maintenance program as the top financial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.07 Tm (risk, because it forces a reactive shop that likely spends more. The diagnostic is blunt: if only 25% of 100 annual work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.85 Tm (orders are preventive or predictive, 75% are breakdowns, major repairs, or surprises [sNcACw9iXI0 @ 00:13:15].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 280.62 Tm (Aubin also reports from CFMA heavy construction committee polls that only 20% of contractors run a work order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 265.40 Tm (system, calling it low-hanging fruit [sNcACw9iXI0 @ 00:20:33], and warns that buying seven significant pieces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 250.17 Tm (without fleet in the room, and without enough mechanics, turns the program reactive. Equipment & Contracting puts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.95 Tm (the field version plainly: nobody wants the key crane dying halfway through the job, and neglected routine maintenance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 219.72 Tm (ends in expensive repairs or outright replacement [HIhx8sY-aac @ 00:01:42]. The Profitable Contractor shows how) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 204.50 Tm (quietly rentals and material creep bleed a job. In its illustration, a $200-a-day rental budgeted for five days runs ten,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 189.27 Tm (costing $2,000 against a $1,000 allowance; with materials creeping from $8,000 to $8,400, the job lands at $13,400) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 174.05 Tm (against a $12,000 budget and gross profit drops $1,400 [jLx7fLatA3A @ 00:06:30]. Charging a shared machine's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.82 Tm (whole bill to one job distorts every project involved, so split it by logged days or hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 143.60 Tm (Fleet control also breaks at the driver seat. thatDOTcop inspected a driver who logged 30 to 35 miles of personal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 128.37 Tm (conveyance to buy a sandwich at a spot closer to the next pickup; on paper it looked personal, but PC cannot be used to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 113.15 Tm (advance the load [zKmff6X7cQA @ 00:04:02]. The driver had no idea, and it became a teaching moment rather than a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 97.92 Tm (citation. Inspectors audit PC through GPS, distances, and timestamps in the eRODS view, and abuse can be written up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 82.70 Tm (as hours-of-service violations under falsified logs, triggering deeper inspections or out-of-service orders) Tj ET
